1
00:00:27,270 --> 00:00:29,140
Come to Los Angeles.

2
00:00:29,150 --> 00:00:31,070
The sun shines bright.

3
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:33,570
The beaches are wide and inviting.

4
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:37,910
And the orange groves stretch as far as the eye can see.

5
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:39,740
There are jobs aplenty.

6
00:00:39,850 --> 00:00:41,440
Land is cheap.

7
00:00:41,590 --> 00:00:44,020
Every workingman can have his own house.

8
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:48,720
And inside every house, a happy all-American family.

9
00:00:48,860 --> 00:00:50,550
You can have all this.

10
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:52,060
And who knows?

11
00:00:52,230 --> 00:00:54,160
You could even be discovered

12
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:55,770
become a movie star,

13
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:57,760
or at least see one.

14
00:00:57,870 --> 00:01:00,560
Life is good in Los Angeles.

15
00:01:00,670 --> 00:01:03,440
It's paradise on earth.

16
00:01:04,780 --> 00:01:07,070
That's what they tell you, anyway.

17
00:01:07,180 --> 00:01:09,170
Because they're selling an image.

18
00:01:09,310 --> 00:01:13,080
They're selling it through movies, radio and television.

19
00:01:13,250 --> 00:01:14,980
In the hit show, Badge of Honor,

20
00:01:15,090 --> 00:01:17,110
the L.A. cops walk on water

21
00:01:17,290 --> 00:01:19,720
as they keep the city clean of crooks.

22
00:01:19,860 --> 00:01:23,330
You'd think this place was the Garden of Eden.

23
00:01:23,390 --> 00:01:25,760
But there's trouble in paradise

24
00:01:25,860 --> 00:01:28,630
and his name is Meyer Harris Cohen,

25
00:01:28,730 --> 00:01:30,560
Mickey C, to his fans.

26
00:01:30,670 --> 00:01:33,190
Local L.A. color to the nth degree.

27
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:35,900
And his number one bodyguard

28
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,670
Johnny Stompanato.

29
00:01:37,810 --> 00:01:40,830
Mickey C's the head of organized crime in these parts.

30
00:01:40,980 --> 00:01:43,970
He runs dope, rackets and prostitution.

31
00:01:44,110 --> 00:01:46,550
He kills a dozen people a year.

32
00:01:46,650 --> 00:01:49,880
And the dapper little gent does it in style.

33
00:01:49,990 --> 00:01:53,080
And every time his picture's on the front page

34
00:01:53,220 --> 00:01:56,320
it's a black eye for the image of Los Angeles.

35
00:01:56,460 --> 00:01:58,950
Because how can organized crime exist

36
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:02,460
in the city with the best police force in the world?

37
00:02:02,570 --> 00:02:04,060
Something has to be done.

38
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:05,400
But nothing too original, because, hey, this is Hollywood.

39
00:02:07,670 --> 00:02:10,770
What worked for Al Capone would work for the Mickster.

40
00:02:10,910 --> 00:02:12,540
Mr. Cohen, you're under arrest.

41
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:15,440
Nonpayment of federal income tax.

42
00:02:15,550 --> 00:02:17,170
But all is not well.

43
00:02:17,350 --> 00:02:19,610
Sending Mickey up has created a vacuum.

44
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:22,560
And it's only a matter of time

45
00:02:22,570 --> 00:02:25,420
before someone with balls of brass tries to fill it.

46
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:28,790
"Remember, dear readers

47
00:02:28,890 --> 00:02:31,450
you heard it here first

48
