00:15:16,830 --> 00:15:17,950
Get him, Stens!

272
00:15:19,130 --> 00:15:20,560
This is for ours, Poncho.

273
00:15:21,830 --> 00:15:22,860
Get him, Stens!

274
00:15:24,130 --> 00:15:25,120
Let me through!

275
00:15:27,140 --> 00:15:28,100
No! He didn't do nothing!

276
00:15:28,240 --> 00:15:30,140
What are you looking at?

277
00:15:31,710 --> 00:15:32,830
Tell that Mexican to shut up!

278
00:15:34,540 --> 00:15:35,480
You're sick!

279
00:15:42,190 --> 00:15:45,550
Don't break it up. Get back! Get back!

280
00:15:46,420 --> 00:15:47,390
Yeah, and fuck your mother!

281
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:48,580
Fuck you!

282
00:15:52,230 --> 00:15:53,820
Stop, officer! That's an order!

283
00:16:02,610 --> 00:16:03,870
You'll all be in my report!

284
00:16:24,190 --> 00:16:25,990
"Bloody Christmas."

285
00:16:26,100 --> 00:16:27,930
The press love to label.

286
00:16:29,700 --> 00:16:32,500
You should know this is bigger than the police board.

287
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:34,540
The grand jury's convening.

288
00:16:34,670 --> 00:16:36,900
Indictments may be handed down.

289
00:16:37,010 --> 00:16:38,530
Will you testify?

290
00:16:38,670 --> 00:16:40,110
No, sir. I won't.

291
00:16:42,850 --> 00:16:44,780
District Attorney Loew?

292
00:16:44,910 --> 00:16:48,820
You and officer Stensland brought the liquor to the station.

293
00:16:48,950 --> 00:16:51,480
Stensland was already drunk.

294
00:16:51,620 --> 00:16:54,060
Appearing as a voluntary witness against him

295
00:16:54,190 --> 00:16:57,060
could offset damage to yourself.

296
00:16:57,190 --> 00:16:58,790
I won't testify against him,

297
00:16:58,930 --> 00:17:00,020
or anyone else.

298
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:02,630
This man is a disgrace.

299
00:17:02,730 --> 00:17:04,430
Your badge and gun, officer.

300
00:17:04,570 --> 00:17:06,360
You're suspended from duty.

301
00:17:07,770 --> 00:17:08,960
Dismissed.

302
00:17:25,460 --> 00:17:31,220
We need police witnesses to offset the damage done to the Department.

303
00:17:31,230 --> 00:17:32,850
Justice has to be served.

304
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:34,090
Of course I'll testify.

305
00:17:37,700 --> 00:17:39,360
I'm glad you feel that way, Edmund.

306
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:40,630
Most don't.

307
00:17:40,770 --> 00:17:43,760
They think silence and integrity are the same thing.

308
00:17:43,910 --> 00:17:49,110
Not exactly the image of the new LAPD we're trying to create.

309
00:17:49,110 --> 00:17:52,280
Welcome to Los Angeles, the city of the future.

310
00:17:52,420 --> 00:17:53,750
-May I make a suggestion, sir?

311
00:17:53,850 --> 00:17:55,040
-By all means.

312
00:17:55,180 --> 00:18:00,090
The public will expect the Department to sweep this under the carpet.

313
00:18:00,260 --> 00:18:01,660
Don't.

314
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:05,060
Shift the guilt to men whose pensions are secured.

315
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:06,690
Force them to retire.

316
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:10,030
But somebody has to swing.

317
00:18:10,130 --> 00:18:15,830
So indict, try and convict Richard Stensland and Bud White.

318
00:18:15,940 --> 00:18:17,600
Secure them jail time.

319
00:18:17,740 --> 00:18:19,800
The message will be clear.

320
00:18:19,940 --> 00:18:21,500
This Department

321
00:18:21,510 --> 00:18:25,610
will not tolerate officers who think they're above the law.

322
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:29,050
Dick Stensland is an embarrassment as a policeman.

323
00:18:29,150 --> 00:18:33,280
He's had rotten fitness reports from every C.O. he's served under.

324
00:18:33,420 --> 00:18:35,550
But Bud White is a valuable officer.

325
00:18:35,690 --> 00:18:37,320
White's a mindless thug.

326
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:39,330
No, Edmund

327
00:18:39,430 --> 00:18:43,990
but he can answer "yes" to those questions I've asked you before.

328
00:18:44,130 --> 00:18:46,600
The Department and the public need role models.

329
00:18:46,740 --> 00:18:50,360
Clean-cut, forthright men the public can admire.

330
00:18:52,040 --> 00:18:56,910
Sergeant I'll promote you to lieutenant

331
00:18:57,010 --> 00:18:58,450
effective immediately.

332
00:18:58,550 --> 00:19:00,070
Detective Lieutenant.

333
00:19:02,320 --> 00:19:03,950
Ed, you're 30.

334
00:19:04,090 --> 00:19:07,650
Your father didn't make lieutenant till he was 33.

335
00:19:07,790 --> 00:19:09,160
I know that, sir.

336
00:19:09,330 --> 00:19:11,850
When he made lieutenant, it was as a detective.

337
00:19:11,990 --> 00:19:14,430
Before we start polishing our laurels

338
00:19:14,530 --> 00:19:17,520
it'd look better if we had a corroborative witness.

339
00:19:17,670 --> 00:19:19,570
That won't be easy to come by.

340
00:19:19,670 --> 00:19:21,190
The men hate a stool pigeon.

341
00:19:21,370 --> 00:19:23,170
Jack Vincennes.

342
00:19:23,340 --> 00:19:26,170
He hit one of the Mexicans.

343
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:30,210
A veteran like Vincennes might be willing to admit his own culpability

344
00:19:30,510 --> 00:19:33,410
but he'd never rat out a fellow officer.

345
00:19:33,520 --> 00:19:36,490
Jack's the technical advisor on Badge of Honor.

346
00:19:36,620 --> 00:19:38,140
He lives for it.

347
00:19:38,350 --> 00:19:39,950
That's how to get to him.

348
00:19:43,460 --> 00:19:45,390
I'd like you to observe, Ed.

349
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:51,530
Call Sergeant Vincennes.

350
00:19:51,670 --> 00:19:53,430
Bright kid.

351
00:19:53,540 --> 00:19:55,560
You may reap the benefit

352
00:19:55,710 --> 00:19:58,900
but are you ready to be despised in the Department?

353
00:19:59,040 --> 00:20:00,470
Yes, sir, I am.

354
00:20:02,550 --> 00:20:03,940
So be it.

355
00:20:09,920 --> 00:20:12,440
Sergeant, we'll get right to it.

356
00:20:12,590 --> 00:20:16,620
Nine civilian witnesses have identified you as hitting Ezekiel Garcia.

357
00:20:16,760 --> 00:20:19,950
But we have a witness who will name names

358
00:20:20,130 --> 00:20:23,000
and testify that you hit back

359
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:24,090
only after being hit.

360
00:20:24,230 --> 00:20:27,780
You will testify against 3 officers

361
00:20:27,790 --> 00:20:31,570
who have earned their pensions and plead ignorance about the rest.

362
00:20:31,670 --> 00:20:33,670
No thanks. I'm not a snitch.

363
00:20:33,810 --> 00:20:36,210
I'll guarantee you a slap on the wrist, a brief suspension

364
00:20:36,310 --> 00:20:41,150
followed by a temporary transfer from Narcotics to Vice.

365
00:20:41,250 --> 00:20:43,880
You transfer out of Vice, you'll be back on the show.

366
00:20:49,030 --> 00:20:50,390
The show?

367
00:20:50,490 --> 00:20:52,760
Badge of Honor, Vincennes.

368
00:20:53,860 --> 00:20:57,460
We need to tone down your profile for a bit.

369
00:20:57,600 --> 00:21:02,060
I doubt you've ever taken a stupid breath.

370
00:21:02,070 --> 00:21:03,730
Don't start now.

371
00:21:03,870 --> 00:21:05,310
Okay, I'll do it.

372
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:12,970
The grand jury will hear your testimony tomorrow.

373
00:21:24,330 --> 00:21:28,530
And so it goes Detective Lieutenant.

374
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:32,500
Ace them at the grand jury tomorrow, son.

375
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:36,470
Wear a smart-looking suit and ace them.

376
00:21:36,570 --> 00:21:39,670
And Ed lose the glasses.

377
00:21:50,020 --> 00:21:52,850
So you're the stellar witness.

378
00:21:52,960 --> 00:21:54,450
I should have known.

379
00:21:54,590 --> 00:21:56,850
What's the Chief throwing you?

380
00:21:56,960 --> 00:21:58,220
Throwing me?

381
00:21:58,330 --> 00:22:00,260
Yeah, Exley, what's the payoff?

382
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:02,520
You're the payoff expert.

383
00:22:02,670 --> 00:22:03,630
I'm just doing my duty.

384
00:22:03,770 --> 00:22:07,500
Come on, you're playing an angle here, college boy.

385
00:22:07,600 --> 00:22:08,570
You'll get something so you don't have to hobnob with the cops

386
00:22:08,700 --> 00:22:13,000
who'll hate you for snitching.

387
00:22:13,110 --> 00:22:16,040
If they're making you detective, watch out.

388
00:22:16,180 --> 00:22:18,310
Some Bureau guys will burn in this

389
00:22:18,450 --> 00:22:20,510
and you'll be working with their friends.

390
00:22:20,650 --> 00:22:22,120
What about you?

391
00:22:22,250 --> 00:22:23,510
I'm snitching 3 old-timers

392
00:22:23,620 --> 00:22:26,610
who'll be fishing in Oregon next week.

393
00:22:26,760 --> 00:22:28,850
Next to you, I'm clean

394
00:22:28,990 --> 00:22:30,390
and smart.

395
00:22:30,530 --> 00:22:32,860
Edmund J. Exley to chambers.

396
00:22:35,300 --> 00:22:36,290
And remember

397
00:22:36,430 --> 00:22:39,360
Bud White will fuck you for this if it takes the rest of his life.

398
00:22:44,210 --> 00:22:46,570
Captain, what do you want?

399
00:22:46,680 --> 00:22:48,110
Call me Dudley.

400
00:22:48,210 --> 00:22:52,610
Dudley what do you want?

401
00:22:52,750 --> 00:22:53,940
Look, lad,

402
00:22:54,080 --> 00:22:56,570
I admire your refusal to testify

403
00:22:56,720 --> 00:22:59,090
and your loyalty to your partner.

404
00:22:59,190 --> 00:23:01,250
I admire you as a policeman

405
00:23:01,390 --> 00:23:05,320
and your adherence to violence as a necessary adjunct to the job.

406
00:23:06,030 --> 00:23:09,370
I'm impressed with your punishment of women-beaters.

407
00:23:10,370 --> 00:23:11,990
Do you hate them, Wendell?

408
00:23:14,100 --> 00:23:15,570
What do you want?

409
00:23:19,910 --> 00:23:21,040
They're yours.

410
00:23:22,710 --> 00:23:23,840
Take them.

411
00:23:27,220 --> 00:23:28,680
There's no bill on me?

412
00:23:28,820 --> 00:23:30,810
-4 witnesses recanted their testimony.

413
00:23:30,950 --> 00:23:33,050
-Why? They had a change of heart.

414
00:23:33,190 --> 00:23:34,210
Stensland?

415
00:23:34,360 --> 00:23:36,120
Your partner's through.

416
00:23:36,230 --> 00:23:38,490
Scapegoat on the Chief's orders.

417
00:23:38,630 --> 00:23:40,750
A year from his pension.

418
00:23:43,730 --> 00:23:46,790
-Exley! -Exley got what he wanted.

419
00:23:46,940 --> 00:23:50,900
As a politician he exceeds even myself.

420
00:23:51,040 --> 00:23:54,410
The Department needs smart men like Exley

421
00:23:54,510 --> 00:23:58,140
and direct men like you.

422
00:23:59,280 --> 00:24:03,450
Look, I need you for an assignment the Chief's given me.

423
00:24:03,620 --> 00:24:06,050
A duty few men are fit for

424
00:24:06,160 --> 00:24:08,210
but you were born for.

425
00:24:08,360 --> 00:24:11,120
You'd be working out of Homicide at City Hall.

426
00:24:11,230 --> 00:24:13,320
Homicide?

427
00:24:13,460 --> 00:24:14,860
Working cases?

428
00:24:16,170 --> 00:24:19,230
Your talents lie elsewhere, Wendell.

429
00:24:19,370 --> 00:24:22,000
It's a muscle job.

430
00:24:22,140 --> 00:24:25,130
You'll do as I say and ask no questions.

431
00:24:25,310 --> 00:24:27,430
Do you follow my drift?

432
00:24:27,640 --> 00:24:29,080
In Technicolor, sir.

433
00:24:31,950 --> 00:24:35,080
"Meet Tony Brancato and Anthony Trombino

434
00:24:35,220 --> 00:24:38,550
two rising lieutenants in the Mickey Cohen rackets.

435
00:24:38,690 --> 00:24:40,950
With the dapper little gent in prison

436
00:24:41,060 --> 00:24:43,620
who knows how far they'll go.

437
00:24:43,630 --> 00:24:45,430
The sky's the limit.

438
00:24:52,070 --> 00:24:53,060
Oh, well."

439
00:25:06,220 --> 00:25:07,840
"Meet Deuce Perkins,

440
00:25:07,980 --> 00:25:10,470
Mickey Cohen's narcotics lieutenant.

441
00:25:10,690 --> 00:25:12,780
Could he be behind the hits?

442
00:25:12,920 --> 00:25:16,020
Is he consolidating organized crime power?

443
00:25:21,930 --> 00:25:23,630
I suppose not.

444
00:25:29,140 --> 00:25:30,540
One thing's for sure:

445
00:25:30,710 --> 00:25:34,110
2-man triggers are punching the tickets on the Mickster's muscle."

446
00:25:43,450 --> 00:25:47,360
Meanwhile, rumor has it the LAPD

447
00:25:47,360 --> 00:25:52,260
has set up a not-so-Welcome Wagon to dishearten the criminal element

448
00:25:52,360 --> 00:25:55,760
from filling the void left by Mickey's absence.

449
00:25:55,900 --> 00:25:57,530
When I know more,

450
00:25:57,670 --> 00:25:59,030
dear readers, so will you.

451
00:25:59,130 --> 00:26:05,970
Off the record, on the q.t and very Hush-Hush."

452
00:26:07,040 --> 00:26:11,310
With Mickey Cohen in prison, Los Angeles is organized crime-free.

453
00:26:11,410 --> 00:26:13,380
The Chief wants to keep it that way.

454
00:26:14,450 --> 00:26:17,580
In Cleveland, you're an organized crime associate

455
00:26:17,750 --> 00:26:21,050
in desperate need of re-education in the ways of polite society.

456
00:26:23,990 --> 00:26:25,590
I hear things.

457
00:26:25,760 --> 00:26:27,820
Like those 2-men shooter teams.

458
00:26:27,960 --> 00:26:30,800
They're 86ing Cohen's lieutenants.

459
00:26:30,810 --> 00:26:32,630
What do you want?

460
00:26:32,800 --> 00:26:34,430
We want you to go home.

461
00:26:39,170 --> 00:26:40,970
Picture-book smut, men.

462
00:26:41,080 --> 00:26:44,740
There's been a bunch of this found at crime scenes lately.

463
00:26:44,880 --> 00:26:50,910
Quality ranges from piss-poor to very well done.

464
00:26:51,050 --> 00:26:53,720
Look who's back from suspension.

465
00:26:53,860 --> 00:26:56,120
We're honored, Sergeant Jack.

466
00:26:56,230 --> 00:26:59,750
Look at that. The Great Jerk-Off Case of 1953.

467
00:26:59,900 --> 00:27:02,390
Is there someplace you'd rather be?

468
00:27:02,530 --> 00:27:03,520
Yeah, working Narcotics,

469
00:27:03,670 --> 00:27:05,830
looking for Cohen's missing H.

470
00:27:05,970 --> 00:27:08,270
Yeah, finding 25 pounds of heroin

471
00:27:08,370 --> 00:27:10,340
would get you plenty of ink.

472
00:27:10,470 --> 00:27:12,960
You should've thought of that before Bloody Christmas.

473
00:27:14,540 --> 00:27:16,480
Make a major case.

474
00:27:16,610 --> 00:27:18,550
It's the only way you'll get out of here.

475
00:27:19,850 --> 00:27:21,410
Dismissed, gentlemen.

476
00:27:29,460 --> 00:27:31,390
Go get the facts, Jack.

477
00:27:31,490 --> 00:27:33,590
Just the facts.

478
00:27:41,040 --> 00:27:42,470
Whatever you desire.

479
00:27:42,600 --> 00:27:45,230
Hi. I'd like to get a delivery to Beverly Hills.

480
00:27:45,370 --> 00:27:47,210
I don't know you.

481
00:27:47,310 --> 00:27:49,370
A friend just gave me this number

482
00:27:49,510 --> 00:27:51,140
and I wanted to find out if

483
00:27:52,920 --> 00:27:56,010
Would you grab a reverse directory and shag a name and address for me?

484
00:27:57,020 --> 00:27:58,540
Crestview-2239.

485
00:28:06,430 --> 00:28:08,690
Hush-Hush, off the record and on the q.t.

486
00:28:08,860 --> 00:28:10,830
Sid, it's Vincennes.

487
00:28:10,970 --> 00:28:12,990
Jackie, you back on narco?

488
00:28:13,140 --> 00:28:14,190
I need some good copy.

489
00:28:14,340 --> 00:28:16,500
I have something going with Vice.

490
00:28:16,640 --> 00:28:18,370
Something juicy for the Sidster?

491
00:28:18,510 --> 00:28:20,940
Tracking porn. Arty, high-class stuff.

492
00:28:21,080 --> 00:28:22,540
Know about Fleur-de-Lis?

493
00:28:22,680 --> 00:28:24,110
Slogan's "Whatever you desire."

494
00:28:24,210 --> 00:28:26,180
No, I've heard burkes.

495
00:28:26,320 --> 00:28:27,710
Get me some narco skinny.

496
00:28:27,880 --> 00:28:29,780
I want to do an all-hophead issue.

497
00:28:29,920 --> 00:28:32,720
Shvartze jazz musicians and movie stars. You like it?

498
00:28:32,820 --> 00:28:35,710
I'll talk to you later.

499
00:28:35,720 --> 00:28:36,600
-What do you got?

500
00:28:36,610 --> 00:28:38,250
-The number's not assigned. Sir.

501
00:28:38,390 --> 00:28:39,380
Thanks, Ginger.

502
00:28:41,800 --> 00:28:42,960
A bootleg.

503
00:28:52,010 --> 00:28:53,340
Take it easy.

504
00:28:53,440 --> 00:28:54,970
Tough break, Stens.

505
00:28:55,110 --> 00:28:57,140
We're going to miss you.

506
00:28:57,280 --> 00:28:58,910
Raw deal, Stensland.

507
00:29:02,520 --> 00:29:04,080
Here comes the snitch.

508
00:29:15,400 --> 00:29:17,330
Sorry about that, Lieutenant.

509
00:29:34,080 --> 00:29:35,410
Stay out of trouble, Bud.

510
00:29:38,420 --> 00:29:39,790
I got a few hours.

511
00:29:39,890 --> 00:29:40,790
I'll buy you a drink.

512
00:29:40,890 --> 00:29:42,690
Rain check. I got a hot date.

513
00:29:44,860 --> 00:29:47,350
Who is she and what did you arrest her for?

514
00:29:47,500 --> 00:29:49,050
It's confidential.

515
00:29:49,200 --> 00:29:52,530
Like that magazine that Vincennes scams for.

516
00:29:52,630 --> 00:29:54,000
Hush-Hush.

517
00:29:55,300 --> 00:29:56,640
I'll see you later in the week.

518
00:29:57,740 --> 00:29:59,670
We'll do the town, on me.

519
00:29:59,810 --> 00:30:02,680
Yeah. I'll bring my wallet just in case.

520
00:30:07,280 --> 00:30:08,410
-See you tomorrow.

521
00:30:08,550 --> 00:30:10,110
-Hold on!

522
00:30:10,250 --> 00:30:11,510
I'll walk down with you.

523
00:30:20,300 --> 00:30:23,960
Punk kid. Who is he trying to impress?

524
00:30:24,100 --> 00:30:25,230
Yeah, I wonder.

525
00:30:25,370 --> 00:30:27,230
Got himself a real career going.

526
00:30:31,870 --> 00:30:34,000
Sergeant Williams, pick up, please.

527
00:30:35,510 --> 00:30:36,840
Sergeant Williams?

528
00:30:40,450 --> 00:30:42,970
Is there anybody up there in Homicide?

529
00:30:44,250 --> 00:30:45,580
Anybody there?

530
00:30:48,060 --> 00:30:49,150
Lieutenant Exley.

531
00:30:49,290 --> 00:30:51,850
You've got a homicide downtown.

532
00:30:52,030 --> 00:30:53,460
-The Nite Owl Coffee Shop.

533
00:30:53,560 --> 00:30:54,590
-I got it.

534
00:31:07,680 --> 00:31:08,840
At least one person's dead.

535
00:31:09,040 --> 00:31:10,480
I stopped for coffee.

536
00:31:10,610 --> 00:31:12,050
No one comes through the front door. Understand?

537
00:31:12,150 --> 00:31:14,120
Understand?

538
00:32:49,540 --> 00:32:52,100
I want barricades at both ends of the street. Make sure--

539
00:32:53,780 --> 00:32:56,270
I took the call. It's my case.

540
00:32:56,420 --> 00:32:57,440
You don't want it

541
00:32:57,590 --> 00:32:58,710
and you can't have it.

542
00:32:58,850 --> 00:32:59,880
I took the call.

543
00:33:00,020 --> 00:33:02,120
It's mine.

544
00:33:02,260 --> 00:33:03,820
I'll make you my second-in-command.

545
00:33:03,960 --> 00:33:06,590
Captain, over here, please.

546
00:33:10,400 --> 00:33:12,800
The cook drew a gun and set it off.

547
00:33:12,900 --> 00:33:14,490
The rest died in the men's room.

548
00:33:19,470 --> 00:33:24,610
Sir we got a total of 15 spent 12-gauge Remington shotgun shells.

549
00:33:24,610 --> 00:33:27,340
I'm betting 3 men, 5-shot capacity pumps,

550
00:33:27,480 --> 00:33:28,640
all of them emptying once.

551
00:33:28,780 --> 00:33:31,720
Excuse me, we got an I.D. on one of the victims.

552
00:33:32,520 --> 00:33:34,220
It's Dick Stensland.

553
00:33:36,630 --> 00:33:39,320
At first, I thought she was Rita Hayworth.

554
00:33:39,460 --> 00:33:40,860
Yeah, me too.

555
00:33:50,570 --> 00:33:52,560
Hell of a way to avoid prison.

556
00:34:03,420 --> 00:34:05,220
What happened?

557
00:34:05,320 --> 00:34:07,810
Appears 3 men held up a coffee shop.

558
00:34:07,960 --> 00:34:11,080
The guy at the register pulled a.38, so they killed him.

559
00:34:11,260 --> 00:34:14,460
Then they killed everyone else.

560
00:34:15,960 --> 00:34:18,900
Lieutenant, we're ready with that Nite Owl I.D.

561
00:34:24,670 --> 00:34:27,070
Is this your daughter?

562
00:34:27,180 --> 00:34:29,540
I don't know.

563
00:34:29,640 --> 00:34:30,800
We know this is difficult.

564
00:34:30,950 --> 00:34:32,540
Take your time.

565
00:34:34,080 --> 00:34:36,240
It seems like my Susan.

566
00:34:36,380 --> 00:34:39,580
But my Susan was a blonde, not a redhead.

567
00:34:39,720 --> 00:34:41,810
When was the last time you saw her?

568
00:34:41,960 --> 00:34:44,390
Just before Christmas.

569
00:34:44,530 --> 00:34:46,720
We'd fought. I didn't like her boyfriend.

570
00:34:48,030 --> 00:34:49,050
Mrs. Lefferts

571
00:34:49,200 --> 00:34:52,960
does your daughter have any distinguishing marks?

572
00:34:53,070 --> 00:34:55,800
You got the wrong idea, mister. I'm fine.

573
00:34:56,870 --> 00:35:00,400
She has a birthmark on her hip.

574
00:35:05,910 --> 00:35:10,280
It's her. My baby!

575
00:35:13,590 --> 00:35:15,060
I'm sorry, Mrs. Lefferts.

576
00:35:16,660 --> 00:35:19,130
Who's in charge of this investigation?

577
00:35:19,290 --> 00:35:21,420
Captain Smith and myself. Why?

578
00:35:23,570 --> 00:35:24,960
"The Nite Owl Massacre."

579
00:35:25,070 --> 00:35:26,930
Hyperbole aside

580
00:35:27,040 --> 00:35:30,400
this is a heinous crime that requires swift resolution.

581
00:35:31,710 --> 00:35:32,800
Six victims.

582
00:35:32,940 --> 00:35:35,430
One of them, one of our own. Dick Stensland.

583
00:35:35,980 --> 00:35:38,100
He was a Nite Owl regular,

584
00:35:38,250 --> 00:35:40,440
in the wrong place at the wrong time.

585
00:35:40,580 --> 00:35:42,520
Robbery is the likely motive.

586
00:35:42,620 --> 00:35:47,250
We have rubber glove smears on the register and forensics

587
00:35:47,390 --> 00:35:48,950
tend toward a trio of shooters.

588
00:35:49,090 --> 00:35:51,460
We do have one hot lead.

589
00:35:51,560 --> 00:35:54,090
Three Negro juveniles

590
00:35:54,230 --> 00:35:57,430
were seen discharging shotguns in Griffith Park.

591
00:35:57,570 --> 00:36:00,730
A park ranger I.D.'d them as driving a 1948-1950 Mercury coupe

592
00:36:01,170 --> 00:36:03,600
maroon in color.

593
00:36:03,710 --> 00:36:07,300
An hour ago a canvassing crew found a news vendor

594
00:36:07,440 --> 00:36:09,640
who saw a maroon Merc coupe parked

595
00:36:09,780 --> 00:36:11,640
by the Nite Owl at 1 a.m.

596
00:36:11,750 --> 00:36:16,450
DMV has come up with a registration list of Merc coupes.

597
00:36:16,590 --> 00:36:21,960
48 two-man teams will shake three names apiece.

598
00:36:22,060 --> 00:36:24,550
Interrogations will be led by Lt. Edmund Exley.

599
00:36:28,030 --> 00:36:29,550
Enough on that!

600
00:36:32,700 --> 00:36:34,130
Gentlemen, just go out and get them.

601
00:36:34,240 --> 00:36:37,230
Use all necessary force.

602
00:36:37,410 --> 00:36:40,100
The people of Los Angeles demand it.

603
00:36:40,240 --> 00:36:41,400
Dismissed.

604
00:36:45,080 --> 00:36:46,640
Why not just put a bounty on them?

605
00:36:54,460 --> 00:36:55,750
-Ready to roll?

606
00:36:55,860 --> 00:36:57,480
-You take them, I got something to do.

607
00:36:57,630 --> 00:36:58,180
What if one of these names--?

608
00:36:58,390 --> 00:37:01,450
Get somebody else.

609
00:37:02,160 --> 00:37:04,500
I got our assignments, Big V.

610
00:37:04,600 --> 00:37:07,900
We go by this list, we got zero chance of making this collar.

611
00:37:08,000 --> 00:37:10,030
I got a guy who knows what happens south of Jefferson.

612
00:37:10,170 --> 00:37:11,500
He'll put us at 50-50.

613
00:37:11,610 --> 00:37:13,870
What are you doing?

614
00:37:13,880 --> 00:37:17,100
It's the same sort of thing that got you in trouble before.

615
00:37:17,150 --> 00:37:18,480
I'll take those odds.

616
00:37:22,880 --> 00:37:23,910
We got it from here.

617
00:37:26,490 --> 00:37:28,620
You two should bring along a photographer.

618
00:37:33,960 --> 00:37:35,830
I need an address on a customer of yours.

619
00:37:35,930 --> 00:37:37,120
Her name is Lynn.

620
00:37:37,270 --> 00:37:38,560
-That's all I got to go on?

621
00:37:38,670 --> 00:37:39,600
-Yeah.

622
00:37:39,730 --> 00:37:42,670
You already know who I mean, so cough it up.

623
00:37:42,800 --> 00:37:45,300
There's a billing address and a delivery address.

624
00:38:12,600 --> 00:38:13,970
Are you Pierce Patchett?

625
00:38:15,340 --> 00:38:16,530
I am.

626
00:38:18,140 --> 00:38:20,800
Are you soliciting for police charities?

627
00:38:20,810 --> 00:38:22,970
Last time you called my office.

628
00:38:23,110 --> 00:38:25,840
Go on down to the driveway. We'll talk there.

629
00:38:37,190 --> 00:38:38,160
What can I do for you?

630
00:38:39,690 --> 00:38:41,130
-Where were you last night?

631
00:38:41,230 --> 00:38:43,200
-I was here hosting a party.

632
00:38:45,030 --> 00:38:46,630
Tell me about Dick Stensland.

633
00:38:46,770 --> 00:38:49,260
I don't know him, Mr.--?

634
00:38:49,400 --> 00:38:50,740
Officer White.

635
00:38:51,870 --> 00:38:53,430
You know Sue Lefferts?

636
00:38:53,580 --> 00:38:55,570
You know I do. You saw me with her.

637
00:38:57,580 --> 00:38:59,570
How did you find me?

638
00:38:59,710 --> 00:39:01,050
Nick's Liquor.

639
00:39:01,150 --> 00:39:04,310
This is where Lynn Bracken's booze bills go.

640
00:39:04,450 --> 00:39:05,580
Of course.

641
00:39:08,620 --> 00:39:11,290
Sue Lefferts died at the Nite Owl.

642
00:39:11,430 --> 00:39:12,890
I'm investigating.

643
00:39:15,260 --> 00:39:17,160
Everything all right?

644
00:39:17,270 --> 00:39:18,990
Fine, Phillip, thank you.

645
00:39:23,340 --> 00:39:26,140
What happened to the other guy, Buzz?

646
00:39:26,240 --> 00:39:28,370
Buzz Meeks no longer works for me.

647
00:39:28,540 --> 00:39:29,600
Lefferts looked beat-up Christmas Eve

648
00:39:29,740 --> 00:39:31,180
but didn't act it. Why?

649
00:39:31,280 --> 00:39:33,540
I think she'd been hit in the face with a tennis racket.

650
00:39:33,650 --> 00:39:37,320
She was a big doubles fan.

651
00:39:38,090 --> 00:39:40,680
You're a known associate of a woman killed in a mass murder.

652
00:39:41,960 --> 00:39:44,290
-Want to go downtown to discuss this?

653
00:39:44,660 --> 00:39:46,850
-Is this official?

654
00:39:47,000 --> 00:39:51,120
Somehow I have the feeling this is more personal with you.

655
00:39:54,900 --> 00:39:56,930
All right, then

656
00:39:57,070 --> 00:40:01,240
are you concerned about criminal matters peripheral to the murders?

657
00:40:01,380 --> 00:40:05,350
-Not at the moment. -You're not obligated to report them?

658
00:40:07,580 --> 00:40:10,020
Why were Lefferts' eyes black?

659
00:40:10,120 --> 00:40:12,990
I needed a Rita Hayworth to fill out my little studio.

660
00:40:13,090 --> 00:40:14,250
What little studio?

661
00:40:14,390 --> 00:40:18,260
Well, there's Gardner, Russell, Monroe, Turner.

662
00:40:18,360 --> 00:40:20,950
Lynn Bracken is my Veronica Lake.

663
00:40:21,100 --> 00:40:23,590
I use girls that look like movie stars.

664
00:40:23,730 --> 00:40:26,790
Sometimes I employ a plastic surgeon.

665
00:40:26,940 --> 00:40:30,030
When the work was done, that's when you saw us.

666
00:40:30,170 --> 00:40:32,000
It's why her mom couldn't I.D. her.

667
00:40:33,680 --> 00:40:35,070
Jesus fucking Christ!

668
00:40:35,180 --> 00:40:37,610
No, Pierce Morehouse Patchett.

669
00:40:39,550 --> 00:40:40,980
I sense you're on your best behavior,

670
00:40:41,120 --> 00:40:43,280
but that's all I'm saying.

671
00:40:43,420 --> 00:40:46,480
If you persist, we'll meet with my attorney.

672
00:40:46,650 --> 00:40:48,590
Would you like Lynn Bracken's address?

673
00:40:48,720 --> 00:40:50,850
I got her address.

674
00:40:52,190 --> 00:40:54,350
Find Susan's killer, Mr. White.

675
00:40:54,500 --> 00:40:56,490
I'll give you a handsome reward.

676
00:41:02,070 --> 00:41:03,300
Whatever you desire!

677
00:41:11,850 --> 00:41:13,580
I know you're not asleep.

678
00:41:15,920 --> 00:41:16,980
What do you want?

679
00:41:17,120 --> 00:41:19,380
My 5 bucks.

680
00:41:19,390 --> 00:41:22,080
It was the only one I had.

681
00:41:22,220 --> 00:41:23,710
Right now?

682
00:41:23,860 --> 00:41:26,590
Hey, doll face, tell him to leave us alone.

683
00:41:26,730 --> 00:41:28,160
I understand.

684
00:41:28,260 --> 00:41:29,290
Okay, fine.

685
00:41:30,470 --> 00:41:32,730
Oh, baby

686
00:41:32,870 --> 00:41:34,390
bad news.

687
00:41:34,540 --> 00:41:35,590
You have to go.

688
00:41:35,740 --> 00:41:37,170
Go?

689
00:41:37,310 --> 00:41:39,800
Something very important has come up and you have to go.

690
00:41:40,880 --> 00:41:42,840
I'll make it up to you.

691
00:41:42,980 --> 00:41:44,410
I will, I promise.

692
00:41:44,510 --> 00:41:45,670
Excuse me.

693
00:41:48,220 --> 00:41:49,410
Is it the cops?

694
00:41:54,190 --> 00:41:55,420
Miss Bracken

695
00:41:55,560 --> 00:41:56,720
I'm Officer White.

696
00:41:56,860 --> 00:41:57,980
I've been expecting you,

697
00:41:58,130 --> 00:41:59,530
just not this soon.

698
00:41:59,690 --> 00:42:02,190
Pierce called. He told me what happened to Sue.

699
00:42:02,330 --> 00:42:04,420
Everything all right, doll?

700
00:42:04,570 --> 00:42:06,000
Want me to get rid of him?

701
00:42:06,100 --> 00:42:07,500
Hit the road.

702
00:42:09,300 --> 00:42:11,170
Maybe I will

703
00:42:11,270 --> 00:42:13,140
maybe I won't.

704
00:42:13,240 --> 00:42:15,040
LAPD. Get out of here

705
00:42:15,180 --> 00:42:17,110
or I'll have your wife come get you.

706
00:42:33,430 --> 00:42:35,160
-Officer. -Councilman.

707
00:42:53,620 --> 00:42:54,780
-Would you care for a drink?

708
00:42:54,920 --> 00:42:57,320
-Yeah, Scotch straight.

709
00:43:02,860 --> 00:43:04,550
I was friendly with Sue Lefferts,

710
00:43:04,760 --> 00:43:06,620
but we weren't friends.

711
00:43:06,760 --> 00:43:08,420
Know what I mean?

712
00:43:08,560 --> 00:43:09,890
You sorry she's dead?

713
00:43:12,130 --> 00:43:13,860
Of course I am.

714
00:43:14,000 --> 00:43:15,630
What kind of question is that?

715
00:43:17,910 --> 00:43:20,370
Do you know why Pierce is humoring you?

716
00:43:20,510 --> 00:43:23,030
Use words like that, you might make me mad.

717
00:43:23,180 --> 00:43:24,340
But, do you know?

718
00:43:24,480 --> 00:43:26,540
Yeah, I know.

719
00:43:26,680 --> 00:43:29,340
Patchett's running whores

720
00:43:29,480 --> 00:43:31,980
cut to look like movie stars.

721
00:43:32,120 --> 00:43:33,250
And, judging by his address,

722
00:43:33,390 --> 00:43:35,650
something bigger on the side.

723
00:43:35,820 --> 00:43:37,690
He doesn't want any attention.

724
00:43:37,830 --> 00:43:40,520
That's right. Our motives are selfish

725
00:43:40,660 --> 00:43:41,590
so we're cooperating.

726
00:43:41,700 --> 00:43:44,760
So cooperate. Why was Susan Lefferts at the Nite Owl?

727
00:43:44,900 --> 00:43:47,530
I don't know. I never heard of the Nite Owl till today.

728
00:43:47,670 --> 00:43:48,860
How'd she meet Patchett?

729
00:43:49,000 --> 00:43:50,560
Pierce meets people.

730
00:43:50,710 --> 00:43:52,640
Sue had dreams of Hollywood

731
00:43:52,740 --> 00:43:55,170
and this is how they turned out.

732
00:43:55,310 --> 00:43:57,240
Thanks to Pierce,

733
00:43:57,350 --> 00:43:59,510
we still get to act a little.

734
00:43:59,650 --> 00:44:02,140
Tell me about Pierce.

735
00:44:02,280 --> 00:44:05,450
He's waiting for you to mention money.

736
00:44:05,590 --> 00:44:07,250
Want advice, Miss Bracken?

737
00:44:07,390 --> 00:44:08,950
It's Lynn.

738
00:44:09,090 --> 00:44:11,080
Miss Bracken

739
00:44:11,230 --> 00:44:13,820
don't ever try to fucking bribe me

740
00:44:13,960 --> 00:44:17,400
or I'll have you and Patchett in shit up to your ears.

741
00:44:17,530 --> 00:44:20,020
I remember you from Christmas Eve.

742
00:44:21,140 --> 00:44:24,160
You have a thing for helping women, don't you?

743
00:44:25,270 --> 00:44:27,140
Maybe I'm just fucking curious.

744
00:44:27,240 --> 00:44:29,070
-You say "fuck" a lot.

745
00:44:29,180 --> 00:44:30,640
-You fuck for money.

746
00:44:30,850 --> 00:44:32,040
There's blood on your shirt.

747
00:44:32,180 --> 00:44:34,610
An integral part of your job?

748
00:44:34,720 --> 00:44:36,620
-Yeah. -Do you enjoy it?

749
00:44:36,720 --> 00:44:37,650
When they deserve it.

750
00:44:37,790 --> 00:44:39,450
Did they deserve it today?

751
00:44:41,060 --> 00:44:42,110
I'm not sure.

752
00:44:42,260 --> 00:44:43,190
-But you did it anyway.

753
00:44:43,320 --> 00:44:44,380
-Yeah.

754
00:44:44,530 --> 00:44:47,890
Like the half dozen guys you screwed today.

755
00:44:48,000 --> 00:44:49,900
Actually, it was only two.

756
00:44:52,470 --> 00:44:54,230
You're different, Officer White.

757
00:44:54,370 --> 00:44:55,840
You're the first man in years

758
00:44:55,970 --> 00:44:59,340
who didn't tell me I look like Veronica Lake.

759
00:44:59,440 --> 00:45:01,530
You look better than Veronica Lake.

760
00:45:06,650 --> 00:45:08,080
Pierce Patchett?

761
00:45:09,380 --> 00:45:10,540
He takes a cut of our earnings

762
00:45:10,690 --> 00:45:12,310
and invests it for us.

763
00:45:12,450 --> 00:45:15,750
He doesn't let us use narcotics and he doesn't abuse us.

764
00:45:15,890 --> 00:45:19,880
Can your policeman's mentality grasp those contradictions?

765
00:45:21,900 --> 00:45:24,190
He had you cut to look like Veronica Lake.

766
00:45:24,300 --> 00:45:25,770
No.

767
00:45:25,930 --> 00:45:29,330
I'm really a brunette, but the rest is me.

768
00:45:30,840 --> 00:45:33,000
And that's all the news that's fit to print.

769
00:45:34,680 --> 00:45:36,140
It's nice meeting you.

770
00:45:41,380 --> 00:45:42,250
-I'd like to see you again.

771
00:45:42,350 --> 00:45:43,610
-For a date

772
00:45:43,750 --> 00:45:45,080
or an appointment?

773
00:45:47,020 --> 00:45:48,680
I don't know.

774
00:45:48,820 --> 00:45:50,590
-For a date, I'd know your first name.

775
00:45:50,730 --> 00:45:51,850
-Forget I asked.

776
00:45:53,190 --> 00:45:54,660
It was a mistake.

777
00:46:15,020 --> 00:46:16,070
Leonard Bidwell?

778
00:46:17,650 --> 00:46:19,210
Come down here and talk to us.

779
00:46:21,620 --> 00:46:23,350
How's the left these days?

780
00:46:23,490 --> 00:46:24,420
What's it to you?

781
00:46:24,530 --> 00:46:26,580
I saw you fight Kid Gavilan.

782
00:46:26,730 --> 00:46:28,320
I like your style.

783
00:46:31,030 --> 00:46:33,400
What do you want, Mr. Policeman?

784
00:46:33,500 --> 00:46:34,560
You got a brother in Folsom.

785
00:46:34,700 --> 00:46:36,140
I put him there.

786
00:46:36,240 --> 00:46:37,360
Until 1970.

787
00:46:37,510 --> 00:46:39,740
How'd you like to make it 1960?

788
00:46:39,870 --> 00:46:44,670
I know the judge, and Lieutenant Exley is good friends with the D.A.

789
00:46:45,650 --> 00:46:50,680
We're looking for 3 colored guys who like to shoot shotguns.

790
00:46:50,780 --> 00:46:53,220
One owns a maroon Mercury coupe.

791
00:46:53,350 --> 00:46:54,690
-Want me to snitch?

792
00:46:54,790 --> 00:46:56,350
-Want to buy your brother 10 years?

793
00:46:56,490 --> 00:46:57,460
-It was 10 years, right?

794
00:46:57,660 --> 00:46:58,650
-Yeah, 10 years.

795
00:46:58,790 --> 00:46:59,950
You don't have to say anything,

796
00:47:00,090 --> 00:47:03,860
just look at this list and point.

797
00:47:06,100 --> 00:47:08,360
He's bad, so I'll just tell you.

798
00:47:08,500 --> 00:47:09,970
Sugar Ray Collins.

799
00:47:10,100 --> 00:47:12,660
Drives a maroon '49 coupe.

800
00:47:12,810 --> 00:47:14,210
Beautiful ride.

801
00:47:15,240 --> 00:47:16,230
Don't know about shotguns,

802
00:47:16,380 --> 00:47:19,540
but he gets his thrills killing dogs.

803
00:47:19,710 --> 00:47:21,340
He's righteous trash.

804
00:47:21,480 --> 00:47:23,180
Look at that. It's five minutes from here.

805
00:47:23,320 --> 00:47:24,340
Thanks.

806
00:47:26,920 --> 00:47:28,320
I'll hear from you

807
00:47:29,390 --> 00:47:30,820
about my brother?

808
00:47:30,930 --> 00:47:33,050
Keep it up, Lenny. U p!

809
00:47:39,400 --> 00:47:41,770
There it is. It's in the back.

810
00:47:59,050 --> 00:48:00,380
-One of ours. -Shit,

811
00:48:00,490 --> 00:48:01,680
somebody beat us here!

812
00:48:07,660 --> 00:48:10,860
Damn it! My glasses!

813
00:48:10,970 --> 00:48:12,020
You're kidding!

814
00:48:13,730 --> 00:48:15,260
Well, just don't shoot me.

815
