1085
01:08:55,700 --> 01:08:59,010
That's twice the $50 you got for wrecking his career.

1086
01:08:59,310 --> 01:09:01,440
-Come here, come here.

1087
01:09:01,450 --> 01:09:02,570
-Jesus, don't bring him--

1088
01:09:07,850 --> 01:09:09,650
That's D.A. Loew right there.

1089
01:09:11,720 --> 01:09:12,950
Ok.

1090
01:09:14,730 --> 01:09:16,720
You need a drink?

1091
01:09:16,860 --> 01:09:18,350
Yeah.

1092
01:09:18,500 --> 01:09:20,260
Look after him.

1093
01:09:20,270 --> 01:09:22,990
Matt, this is Jack.

1094
01:09:23,000 --> 01:09:23,800
No secrets between me and him.

1095
01:09:29,540 --> 01:09:32,140
-How you doing? -I'm okay. How're you?

1096
01:09:32,280 --> 01:09:33,580
I'm good.

1097
01:09:36,350 --> 01:09:38,150
Have we met before?

1098
01:09:40,520 --> 01:09:42,580
Yeah.

1099
01:09:42,720 --> 01:09:44,160
Was it at a party?

1100
01:09:44,170 --> 01:09:46,220
It was something like that.

1101
01:09:47,860 --> 01:09:49,450
Fleur-de-Lis party, right?

1102
01:09:50,800 --> 01:09:52,630
Right.

1103
01:09:52,770 --> 01:09:54,560
Fleur-de-Lis.

1104
01:09:54,700 --> 01:09:56,730
"Whatever you desire."

1105
01:09:56,870 --> 01:10:00,050
Dope, hookers that look like movie stars.

1106
01:10:00,060 --> 01:10:02,500
Pierce Patchett has it all.

1107
01:10:02,640 --> 01:10:05,170
You could say that again.

1108
01:10:05,180 --> 01:10:09,010
Pierce, he's not like regular guys.

1109
01:10:09,150 --> 01:10:10,980
I dig him, but

1110
01:10:12,020 --> 01:10:16,050
you know he scares me too.

1111
01:10:16,390 --> 01:10:18,020
Really?

1112
01:10:18,160 --> 01:10:19,820
How?

1113
01:10:20,030 --> 01:10:25,430
When I came out to L.A. this isn't exactly where I saw myself ending up.

1114
01:10:26,300 --> 01:10:29,400
Yeah, well get in line.

1115
01:10:29,540 --> 01:10:31,090
Your courage, kid. Drink up.

1116
01:10:35,910 --> 01:10:38,970
I don't think I should do this.

1117
01:10:39,050 --> 01:10:41,510
It's not like you don't know how.

1118
01:10:41,520 --> 01:10:43,630
Jack's connected to Badge of Honor.

1119
01:10:43,640 --> 01:10:45,880
Pull this off, you'll get a part.

1120
01:10:46,050 --> 01:10:49,650
I smell a comeback, don't you, Jack?

1121
01:10:51,860 --> 01:10:53,160
The D.A.'s free.

1122
01:10:53,290 --> 01:10:55,740
Go introduce yourself. Go on.

1123
01:10:55,750 --> 01:10:59,230
Tell him about the opening on the show.

1124
01:10:59,240 --> 01:11:02,820
I'm pretty sure I can get you a part on this show.

1125
01:11:02,830 --> 01:11:04,660
But that's later on.

1126
01:11:04,800 --> 01:11:09,700
Tonight, go on over there and pretend it's an acting job.

1127
01:11:09,740 --> 01:11:11,180
Like show biz.

1128
01:11:11,280 --> 01:11:12,900
Acting, that's it.

1129
01:11:13,080 --> 01:11:15,970
Right. No one's going to know about this?

1130
01:11:15,980 --> 01:11:17,010
No.

1131
01:11:18,720 --> 01:11:20,880
It'll be our secret.

1132
01:11:24,120 --> 01:11:25,680
-Show biz.

1133
01:11:25,830 --> 01:11:27,220
-That's it. Go on.

1134
01:11:31,200 --> 01:11:32,820
Show biz.

1135
01:11:34,830 --> 01:11:35,960
If Reynolds works his charms,

1136
01:11:36,140 --> 01:11:37,160
which I know he will

1137
01:11:37,300 --> 01:11:40,880
they'll be at the Hollywood Center Motel, room 203.

1138
01:11:40,890 --> 01:11:43,740
Meet me there at midnight for a photo shoot.

1139
01:11:43,840 --> 01:11:46,440
And maybe we can work in the Hollywood sign this time.

1140
01:11:48,210 --> 01:11:51,310
What do you know about Pierce Patchett?

1141
01:11:51,450 --> 01:11:53,080
I know what you know.

1142
01:11:53,220 --> 01:11:53,920
He's rich.

1143
01:11:53,930 --> 01:11:57,360
Invested in the freeways, which'll make him richer.

1144
01:11:57,490 --> 01:11:58,920
Why?

1145
01:11:59,030 --> 01:12:01,620
I just keep hearing rumors, you know.

1146
01:12:01,630 --> 01:12:03,390
High-class porn, drugs,

1147
01:12:03,400 --> 01:12:05,620
hookers that look like movie stars.

1148
01:12:05,770 --> 01:12:07,530
Patchett's what I call twilight.

1149
01:12:07,670 --> 01:12:09,460
He isn't queer or Red.

1150
01:12:09,600 --> 01:12:13,090
He cannot help me in my quest for prime sinnuendo.

1151
01:12:19,080 --> 01:12:22,380
As though Badge of Honor would touch that guy with a 10-foot pole

1152
01:12:23,080 --> 01:12:26,440
after he's been Hush-Hush cover boy twice in one year.

1153
01:12:26,550 --> 01:12:27,910
See you soon.

1154
01:12:27,920 --> 01:12:32,550
Midnight. I guarantee all kinds of illegal activity.

1155
01:13:05,590 --> 01:13:07,760
Another? Yeah.

1156
01:13:51,870 --> 01:13:52,900
Kid?

1157
01:13:59,110 --> 01:14:00,840
Brother.

1158
01:14:00,980 --> 01:14:03,280
Come on, you don't have to do this--

1159
01:14:35,310 --> 01:14:37,810
Thank you for what you did for me

1160
01:14:37,950 --> 01:14:40,610
for killing those animals who raped me.

1161
01:14:40,750 --> 01:14:43,690
Will you thank Officer White for me, please?

1162
01:14:43,790 --> 01:14:44,850
Sure.

1163
01:14:46,430 --> 01:14:50,360
Seeing him come through the door is about the only thing I remember.

1164
01:14:50,500 --> 01:14:51,550
Thank God.

1165
01:14:52,800 --> 01:14:55,600
You remember what time the Negroes left you, right?

1166
01:14:55,740 --> 01:14:56,870
In your statement,

1167
01:14:56,880 --> 01:14:59,030
you said they left you at midnight.

1168
01:14:59,170 --> 01:15:00,540
They might have.

1169
01:15:05,910 --> 01:15:07,380
They "might" have?

1170
01:15:07,510 --> 01:15:09,140
I don't know what time they left me.

1171
01:15:09,320 --> 01:15:11,310
I wanted them dead.

1172
01:15:11,450 --> 01:15:14,910
Would anyone care that they raped a Mexican girl

1173
01:15:15,050 --> 01:15:18,610
if they hadn't killed those white people at the Nite Owl?

1174
01:15:19,230 --> 01:15:21,250
I did what I had to do for justice.

1175
01:15:21,390 --> 01:15:22,260
Inez.

1176
01:15:22,400 --> 01:15:23,830
Exley, over here.

1177
01:15:23,930 --> 01:15:25,760
Smile, Inez.

1178
01:15:25,900 --> 01:15:28,890
Is he your hero?

1179
01:15:29,040 --> 01:15:30,160
Fellas, how about this?

1180
01:15:30,340 --> 01:15:33,000
"Rape Victim Wheeled Out by Nite Owl Hero."

1181
01:15:39,250 --> 01:15:40,970
All they get is Veronica Lake.

1182
01:15:43,680 --> 01:15:45,710
I get Lynn Margaret Bracken.

1183
01:15:57,100 --> 01:15:58,320
"Bisbee?"

1184
01:16:00,370 --> 01:16:01,700
I grew up there.

1185
01:16:04,140 --> 01:16:06,470
I'm going back in a couple of years,

1186
01:16:06,610 --> 01:16:08,670
open up a dress shop.

1187
01:16:10,680 --> 01:16:13,610
The girls in Bisbee need a little glamour.

1188
01:16:19,320 --> 01:16:20,840
Where'd this come from?

1189
01:16:22,690 --> 01:16:25,120
I was 12. My dad went after my mother with a bottle.

1190
01:16:25,260 --> 01:16:26,490
I got in the way.

1191
01:16:28,590 --> 01:16:29,820
So you saved her.

1192
01:16:31,660 --> 01:16:32,930
Not for long.

1193
01:16:36,100 --> 01:16:37,540
-I'm sorry. It's none of my business.

1194
01:16:37,640 --> 01:16:40,070
-He tied me to the radiator.

1195
01:16:40,170 --> 01:16:43,160
I watched him beat my mother to death with a tire iron

1196
01:16:45,780 --> 01:16:47,440
and he left me there.

1197
01:16:49,850 --> 01:16:52,840
Three days before a truant officer found us.

1198
01:16:55,920 --> 01:16:58,050
They never found the old man.

1199
01:17:07,170 --> 01:17:09,690
Is that why you became a cop?

1200
01:17:09,840 --> 01:17:11,730
To get even?

1201
01:17:12,970 --> 01:17:14,030
Maybe.

1202
01:17:16,140 --> 01:17:17,610
Do you like it?

1203
01:17:20,880 --> 01:17:22,070
I used to.

1204
01:17:24,120 --> 01:17:27,420
Now it's all strong-arm, sitting duck stuff.

1205
01:17:28,050 --> 01:17:29,150
If I could

1206
01:17:30,690 --> 01:17:33,420
get a chance to work Homicide

1207
01:17:33,560 --> 01:17:35,490
like a real detective.

1208
01:17:36,800 --> 01:17:40,100
That prick, Exley, he shot the wrong guys.

1209
01:17:40,230 --> 01:17:41,790
Whoever killed Stensland's still around.

1210
01:17:41,930 --> 01:17:44,600
I know it in here. I know it.

1211
01:17:45,540 --> 01:17:47,470
Something's wrong with the Nite Owl.

1212
01:17:47,610 --> 01:17:49,340
I just can't prove it, that's all.

1213
01:17:51,110 --> 01:17:52,700
I'm not smart enough.

1214
01:17:55,010 --> 01:17:57,980
I'm just the guy they bring in to scare the other guy shitless.

1215
01:18:01,550 --> 01:18:02,710
You're wrong.

1216
01:18:03,790 --> 01:18:06,620
You found Patchett. You found me.

1217
01:18:06,760 --> 01:18:08,560
You're smart enough.

1218
01:18:20,270 --> 01:18:22,740
Bud White! What brings you down to the basement?

1219
01:18:27,180 --> 01:18:29,080
I got a couple of Nite Owl questions.

1220
01:18:29,180 --> 01:18:31,240
Don't know if you read the papers,

1221
01:18:31,250 --> 01:18:32,740
but that case is closed.

1222
01:18:34,350 --> 01:18:36,790
Anything bother you about it?

1223
01:18:36,920 --> 01:18:40,380
The fact that the pack-up boys haven't hauled this shit out of here yet.

1224
01:18:45,260 --> 01:18:49,360
The suspects' 3 shotguns match the strike marks on the shell casings.

1225
01:18:50,270 --> 01:18:52,600
What more do you want?

1226
01:19:04,080 --> 01:19:05,410
There's blood on the wall here.

1227
01:19:06,650 --> 01:19:09,090
I thought everyone got shot in the men's room.

1228
01:19:09,190 --> 01:19:11,820
That is Stensland's blood.

1229
01:19:11,960 --> 01:19:13,650
Stensland? Yeah.

1230
01:19:13,790 --> 01:19:14,820
Blow to the head.

1231
01:19:14,960 --> 01:19:17,430
Probably unconscious when they dragged him in the john.

1232
01:19:19,300 --> 01:19:20,390
Did they hit anyone else?

1233
01:19:20,570 --> 01:19:22,170
No, but he was a cop.

1234
01:19:22,180 --> 01:19:23,930
Probably tried to do something.

1235
01:19:27,870 --> 01:19:29,600
Grilled cheese, black coffee.

1236
01:19:29,740 --> 01:19:31,680
Someone was sitting next to him.

1237
01:19:35,450 --> 01:19:37,250
2 victims were women?

1238
01:19:37,380 --> 01:19:40,150
Yeah, Patti DeLuca, the night shift waitress,

1239
01:19:40,160 --> 01:19:41,780
and a Susan Lefferts.

1240
01:19:46,190 --> 01:19:47,680
Susan Lefferts.

1241
01:19:49,600 --> 01:19:50,690
Yeah, what about her?

1242
01:19:54,100 --> 01:19:56,030
You're welcome!

1243
01:19:57,870 --> 01:19:59,200
Mrs. Lefferts

1244
01:20:01,670 --> 01:20:02,770
Mrs. Lefferts?

1245
01:20:02,910 --> 01:20:05,540
I'm Officer White, LAPD.

1246
01:20:07,980 --> 01:20:11,140
Tell me about the boyfriend you mentioned at the coroner's office.

1247
01:20:11,320 --> 01:20:14,290
I told you I didn't approve of that boyfriend.

1248
01:20:14,420 --> 01:20:16,350
He was too old for you.

1249
01:20:16,460 --> 01:20:18,550
And you let him be fresh with me.

1250
01:20:20,560 --> 01:20:23,430
They came here one day when I wasn't home.

1251
01:20:23,500 --> 01:20:25,430
Mrs. Jensen next door said

1252
01:20:25,560 --> 01:20:28,290
she saw Susie's boyfriend and another man and

1253
01:20:28,670 --> 01:20:31,530
she heard a ruckus.

1254
01:20:31,900 --> 01:20:33,130
What was his name?

1255
01:20:33,270 --> 01:20:36,300
We weren't properly introduced.

1256
01:20:36,440 --> 01:20:38,970
Susie gave him a nickname, Muns or Luns.

1257
01:20:39,110 --> 01:20:40,510
Stens?

1258
01:20:40,650 --> 01:20:41,700
Was it Stens?

1259
01:20:41,850 --> 01:20:43,080
Maybe.

1260
01:20:43,220 --> 01:20:44,240
I don't know.

1261
01:20:44,380 --> 01:20:45,580
Look.

1262
01:20:49,090 --> 01:20:50,110
That's him.

1263
01:20:50,260 --> 01:20:52,050
That's him.

1264
01:20:57,060 --> 01:20:58,790
You said a neighbor heard a ruckus.

1265
01:20:59,900 --> 01:21:02,460
Was it outside? Inside?

1266
01:21:03,200 --> 01:21:04,460
Outside.

1267
01:21:04,600 --> 01:21:09,130
And then Mrs. Jensen said they kept going under the house.

1268
01:21:12,780 --> 01:21:15,570
You have to leave now, officer.

1269
01:21:16,450 --> 01:21:17,180
-What's through here?

1270
01:21:17,320 --> 01:21:20,110
-Just a room full of old things.

1271
01:21:20,250 --> 01:21:21,480
Don't move that!

1272
01:21:24,520 --> 01:21:25,320
Don't mind the smell.

1273
01:21:25,460 --> 01:21:27,720
I think a rat died behind the wall.

1274
01:21:29,500 --> 01:21:31,430
My Susie was a good girl.

1275
01:21:31,560 --> 01:21:34,230
She was never in any kind of trouble at all!

1276
01:22:46,010 --> 01:22:48,270
"Leland Meeks." Never heard of you.

1277
01:22:48,410 --> 01:22:50,570
They call me Buzz.

1278
01:22:57,220 --> 01:22:59,150
Was it a rat?

1279
01:22:59,250 --> 01:23:00,980
Yeah, a great big one.

1280
01:23:03,520 --> 01:23:05,350
Here.

1281
01:23:05,490 --> 01:23:07,360
Compliments of the Police Department.

1282
01:23:24,480 --> 01:23:27,470
Stomach of the week from a motel homicide.

1283
01:23:27,610 --> 01:23:31,330
Unemployed actor had frankfurter, French fries, alcohol and sperm.

1284
01:23:31,340 --> 01:23:34,200
Hell of a last supper, don't you think?

1285
01:23:34,210 --> 01:23:37,380
Anything bothering you about the Nite Owl case?

1286
01:23:37,520 --> 01:23:39,650
That you guys won't let it get filed away.

1287
01:23:40,730 --> 01:23:41,780
-What do you mean?

1288
01:23:41,930 --> 01:23:43,900
-Bud White grilled me on it today.

1289
01:23:45,360 --> 01:23:46,390
Bud White?

1290
01:23:46,530 --> 01:23:49,720
He's not as dumb as I thought.

1291
01:23:51,570 --> 01:23:54,100
Did he say where he was going after he talked to you?

1292
01:24:06,850 --> 01:24:08,650
Let my daughter rest in peace!

1293
01:24:08,790 --> 01:24:10,910
Mrs. Lefferts, I want to ask a few questions.

1294
01:24:11,060 --> 01:24:13,990
Officer White already checked under the house.

1295
01:24:14,130 --> 01:24:15,820
Under the house?

1296
01:24:15,960 --> 01:24:17,900
-Where? -Out back.

1297
01:24:19,700 --> 01:24:21,530
All he found was rodents.

1298
01:24:24,770 --> 01:24:26,700
I need an I.D. on this as soon as possible.

1299
01:24:26,810 --> 01:24:28,240
Talk only to me on this one.

1300
01:24:31,610 --> 01:24:33,170
I need your help.

1301
01:24:33,180 --> 01:24:36,750
I'm busy right now. Why don't you ask your boys in Homicide?

1302
01:24:40,120 --> 01:24:43,520
I can't. I need someone outside of Homicide.

1303
01:24:43,620 --> 01:24:46,310
Tail Bud White until he goes on duty this evening.

1304
01:24:47,760 --> 01:24:50,490
Do me a real favor and leave me alone.

1305
01:24:51,260 --> 01:24:53,290
You make the Negroes for the Nite Owl killings?

1306
01:24:56,640 --> 01:24:57,830
What?

1307
01:24:57,840 --> 01:24:59,800
It's a simple question.

1308
01:25:01,510 --> 01:25:07,010
Why in the world do you want to dig deeper into the Nite Owl killings

1309
01:25:07,020 --> 01:25:08,410
Lieutenant?

1310
01:25:11,780 --> 01:25:12,980
Rollo Tomasi.

1311
01:25:15,350 --> 01:25:17,690
Is there more or do I have to guess?

1312
01:25:20,430 --> 01:25:23,090
Rollo was a purse snatcher.

1313
01:25:27,130 --> 01:25:28,760
My father ran into him off-duty.

1314
01:25:31,140 --> 01:25:34,700
He shot my father 6 times and got away clean.

1315
01:25:35,670 --> 01:25:37,940
No one knew who he was.

1316
01:25:38,380 --> 01:25:40,610
I made the name up to give him personality.

1317
01:25:42,380 --> 01:25:43,940
What's your point?

1318
01:25:44,080 --> 01:25:46,520
Rollo Tomasi's the reason I became a cop.

1319
01:25:47,550 --> 01:25:48,380
I wanted to catch the guys...

1320
01:25:48,520 --> 01:25:50,150
who thought they could get away with it.

1321
01:25:52,460 --> 01:25:54,720
It was supposed to be about justice.

1322
01:25:55,360 --> 01:25:57,990
Then somewhere along the way I lost sight of that.

1323
01:26:02,500 --> 01:26:03,900
Why'd you become a cop?

1324
01:26:14,410 --> 01:26:15,850
I don't remember.

1325
01:26:22,750 --> 01:26:24,690
What do you want, Exley?

1326
01:26:24,790 --> 01:26:26,850
I want to solve this thing.

1327
01:26:27,030 --> 01:26:29,190
Nite Owl was solved.

1328
01:26:29,330 --> 01:26:30,390
No.

1329
01:26:31,560 --> 01:26:33,460
I want to do it right.

1330
01:26:33,570 --> 01:26:36,300
Even if it means paying the consequences?

1331
01:26:39,470 --> 01:26:41,770
All right, college boy, I'll help.

1332
01:26:41,910 --> 01:26:44,470
But there's a case your boys in Homicide don't care about.

1333
01:26:44,610 --> 01:26:48,310
They think it's just another Hollywood "homo"-cide.

1334
01:26:48,320 --> 01:26:49,540
But I don't.

1335
01:26:49,680 --> 01:26:51,170
You help me with mine,

1336
01:26:51,320 --> 01:26:53,250
I'll help you with yours.

1337
01:26:53,350 --> 01:26:55,050
Deal?

1338
01:26:55,150 --> 01:26:56,420
Deal.

1339
01:27:28,550 --> 01:27:30,180
Johnny Stompanato.

1340
01:27:31,720 --> 01:27:34,060
Officer Wendell White. How's tricks, paesano?

1341
01:27:34,690 --> 01:27:37,060
I amn't your paesano.

1342
01:27:37,200 --> 01:27:39,350
I amn't in the snitch business anymore.

1343
01:27:39,360 --> 01:27:41,630
You know a guy named Buzz Meeks?

1344
01:27:42,870 --> 01:27:45,200
Works for Pierce Patchett.

1345
01:27:45,340 --> 01:27:46,630
Should I?

1346
01:27:47,970 --> 01:27:50,500
You're muscle for hire. Meeks is muscle for hire.

1347
01:27:50,640 --> 01:27:52,770
You tell me.

1348
01:27:53,380 --> 01:27:55,940
