Meeks never made an arrest the entire time he worked Vice?

1609
01:45:59,300 --> 01:46:01,070
Someone must've pulled the files.

1610
01:46:04,110 --> 01:46:05,740
What about the daily report books?

1611
01:46:05,880 --> 01:46:08,140
They'd be buried in the basement.

1612
01:46:08,250 --> 01:46:09,410
Find them.

1613
01:46:40,550 --> 01:46:41,530
Did you talk to Exley?

1614
01:46:42,550 --> 01:46:43,740
Come in out of the rain.

1615
01:46:46,180 --> 01:46:47,670
I want to know what happened with Exley.

1616
01:46:50,160 --> 01:46:51,180
Just come in.

1617
01:46:52,920 --> 01:46:55,790
Are you going to tell me what happened with Exley?

1618
01:46:55,890 --> 01:46:57,730
We talked.

1619
01:46:57,830 --> 01:46:59,350
Tell me about him.

1620
01:46:59,530 --> 01:47:02,590
Later.

1621
01:47:05,840 --> 01:47:06,960
You fucked him.

1622
01:47:11,180 --> 01:47:12,140
You fucked him.

1623
01:47:13,280 --> 01:47:14,870
I thought I was helping you.

1624
01:48:06,060 --> 01:48:07,460
I'm glad you're here.

1625
01:48:07,600 --> 01:48:08,930
I need you to see this.

1626
01:48:17,910 --> 01:48:18,930
Wait.

1627
01:48:45,900 --> 01:48:47,800
Dudley killed Jack.

1628
01:48:47,910 --> 01:48:49,270
He wants you to kill me.

1629
01:48:53,010 --> 01:48:55,500
He showed you the photo, didn't he?

1630
01:48:55,650 --> 01:48:56,810
Didn't he?

1631
01:48:59,480 --> 01:49:01,750
Think!! Goddamn you, think!!

1632
01:49:03,760 --> 01:49:05,050
Get out!

1633
01:49:18,770 --> 01:49:19,740
Dudley

1634
01:49:21,670 --> 01:49:23,400
I checked the daily report books.

1635
01:49:24,980 --> 01:49:28,240
Dudley, Buzz Meeks and Stensland go way back.

1636
01:49:32,150 --> 01:49:33,620
I knew Stensland lied to me.

1637
01:49:36,960 --> 01:49:39,720
Lefferts' mother I.D.'d Stensland as Lefferts' boyfriend.

1638
01:49:41,790 --> 01:49:44,280
Stensland pretended he didn't know Meeks...

1639
01:49:44,380 --> 01:49:47,700
or her the night that I met Lynn.

1640
01:49:49,800 --> 01:49:51,700
Stensland and Meeks

1641
01:49:51,800 --> 01:49:53,900
what the hell were they up to?

1642
01:49:54,010 --> 01:49:55,200
I don't know.

1643
01:49:55,340 --> 01:49:58,100
But I think Stens killed Meeks over heroin.

1644
01:49:58,210 --> 01:49:59,440
What heroin?

1645
01:50:05,380 --> 01:50:08,510
Johnny Stompanato told me that Meeks had heroin for sale.

1646
01:50:09,190 --> 01:50:11,180
Meeks ends up dead.

1647
01:50:11,290 --> 01:50:13,280
Stensland dies at the Nite Owl.

1648
01:50:14,560 --> 01:50:15,990
It wasn't the Negroes.

1649
01:50:17,300 --> 01:50:19,660
The rape victim lied in her statement.

1650
01:50:19,760 --> 01:50:23,390
The first guys to the Mercury coupe were Breuning and Carlisle.

1651
01:50:23,500 --> 01:50:25,400
Dudley's guys.

1652
01:50:25,500 --> 01:50:27,200
They planted the shotguns.

1653
01:50:27,310 --> 01:50:28,430
They'd have killed the Negroes too

1654
01:50:28,540 --> 01:50:30,100
if Jack and I hadn't shown up.

1655
01:50:31,780 --> 01:50:35,230
Dudley framed them because they were Negroes and had records.

1656
01:50:35,380 --> 01:50:37,510
He knew there'd be no questions asked

1657
01:50:39,380 --> 01:50:42,620
if they were killed resisting arrest.

1658
01:50:42,750 --> 01:50:45,590
Somehow this is all connected to Jack's angle.

1659
01:50:45,760 --> 01:50:47,550
Sid Hudgens

1660
01:50:47,760 --> 01:50:50,320
the pictures to blackmail Ellis Loew.

1661
01:50:50,430 --> 01:50:53,190
A kid got murdered.

1662
01:50:53,300 --> 01:50:55,630
To figure this out, we need to work together.

1663
01:51:01,340 --> 01:51:02,770
Why are you doing this?

1664
01:51:05,080 --> 01:51:06,410
The Nite Owl made you.

1665
01:51:08,650 --> 01:51:10,080
You want to tear all that down?

1666
01:51:11,880 --> 01:51:14,150
With a wrecking ball.

1667
01:51:14,250 --> 01:51:15,620
Want to help me swing it?

1668
01:51:28,430 --> 01:51:29,800
Let's go see Ellis Loew.

1669
01:51:30,870 --> 01:51:33,100
Find out what the District Attorney knows.

1670
01:51:40,110 --> 01:51:43,340
You can't go in there.

1671
01:51:45,550 --> 01:51:47,210
-Want me to call the police, Mr. Loew?

1672
01:51:47,320 --> 01:51:48,810
-Ask for Capt. Dudley Smith.

1673
01:51:48,920 --> 01:51:50,750
Tell him we're discussing...

1674
01:51:50,850 --> 01:51:52,760
an unemployed actor's death at a Sunset Strip motel.

1675
01:51:52,860 --> 01:51:54,520
These are the police.

1676
01:52:00,830 --> 01:52:01,660
What do you want?

1677
01:52:01,830 --> 01:52:03,770
I want D.A. bureau men to

1678
01:52:03,870 --> 01:52:06,630
tail Dudley Smith and Patchett 24 hours a day.

1679
01:52:06,740 --> 01:52:10,070
I want you to get a judge to authorize wiretaps on their home phones.

1680
01:52:10,210 --> 01:52:13,080
I want authorization to check their bank records.

1681
01:52:13,210 --> 01:52:15,110
On what evidence?

1682
01:52:15,210 --> 01:52:16,610
Call it a hunch.

1683
01:52:18,050 --> 01:52:19,780
Absolutely not.

1684
01:52:19,880 --> 01:52:22,880
Dudley Smith is a highly decorated member of the department.

1685
01:52:22,990 --> 01:52:25,050
I won't smear his and Patchett's name without--

1686
01:52:25,160 --> 01:52:26,950
Without what?

1687
01:52:27,060 --> 01:52:29,190
Them smearing yours first?

1688
01:52:29,290 --> 01:52:30,690
What do they have?

1689
01:52:30,860 --> 01:52:33,130
Pictures of you and Matt Reynolds with your pants down?

1690
01:52:35,430 --> 01:52:36,870
You have any proof?

1691
01:52:36,970 --> 01:52:38,960
The proof had his throat slit.

1692
01:52:40,210 --> 01:52:41,900
So far, you're not denying it.

1693
01:52:43,540 --> 01:52:45,700
I won't dignify this with answers.

1694
01:52:45,880 --> 01:52:48,370
Now if you gentlemen will excuse me

1695
01:52:48,510 --> 01:52:51,680
I have a press conference for Jack Vincennes that I have to prepare for.

1696
01:53:02,730 --> 01:53:04,890
Unless you came to wipe my ass,

1697
01:53:05,000 --> 01:53:06,590
I believe we're through.

1698
01:53:11,240 --> 01:53:13,830
Don't pull that good cop-bad cop crap.

1699
01:53:13,940 --> 01:53:15,130
I practically invented it.

1700
01:53:16,370 --> 01:53:18,740
So what if some homo actor is dead.

1701
01:53:18,880 --> 01:53:21,510
Boys, girls, ten of them get off the bus to L.A. everyday.

1702
01:53:29,920 --> 01:53:31,320
Pull him off me!!

1703
01:53:31,420 --> 01:53:32,860
I don't know how.

1704
01:53:36,290 --> 01:53:38,560
I know you think you're the A-number-one hotshot,

1705
01:53:38,660 --> 01:53:39,530
but here's the juice.

1706
01:53:39,630 --> 01:53:40,490
If I kill you,

1707
01:53:40,500 --> 01:53:42,660
10 lawyers will take your place tomorrow.

1708
01:53:42,770 --> 01:53:44,260
They just won't come on a bus.

1709
01:53:58,820 --> 01:54:00,180
Okay!

1710
01:54:01,490 --> 01:54:02,540
Dudley and Patchett, they.

1711
01:54:04,290 --> 01:54:05,650
Oh, my God!

1712
01:54:05,760 --> 01:54:06,880
I wouldn't play ball

1713
01:54:06,990 --> 01:54:09,390
so they set me up! I gave in!

1714
01:54:09,400 --> 01:54:11,520
But the kid heard everything

1715
01:54:11,630 --> 01:54:12,650
so they killed him.

1716
01:54:12,760 --> 01:54:15,520
Why? -What are Dudley and Patchett up to?

1717
01:54:15,530 --> 01:54:17,660
-Taking over Mickey Cohen's rackets.

1718
01:54:17,770 --> 01:54:21,200
Because of those pictures I couldn't prosecute them!

1719
01:54:22,040 --> 01:54:22,940
Oh, Jesus!

1720
01:54:23,040 --> 01:54:24,770
Help me up!

1721
01:54:33,790 --> 01:54:35,840
Is that how you ran the good cop-bad cop?

1722
01:54:38,460 --> 01:54:39,510
Patchett?

1723
01:55:15,090 --> 01:55:17,460
Looks like his bodyguard had a conflict of interest.

1724
01:55:24,200 --> 01:55:25,530
Suicide note.

1725
01:55:25,640 --> 01:55:29,600
Says he killed Jack because Jack had figured out his pornography scam.

1726
01:55:30,440 --> 01:55:32,530
Slicing himself open wasn't his idea.

1727
01:55:34,110 --> 01:55:35,580
2 of his fingers are broken.

1728
01:55:35,680 --> 01:55:36,870
They held him there.

1729
01:55:38,920 --> 01:55:40,080
Or drugged him.

1730
01:55:43,250 --> 01:55:45,780
Dudley's tying up his loose ends.

1731
01:55:45,890 --> 01:55:47,050
Patchett's dead.

1732
01:55:47,160 --> 01:55:48,850
He sent you after me.

1733
01:55:50,760 --> 01:55:51,820
Lynn.

1734
01:55:53,060 --> 01:55:54,050
West Hollywood Sheriff.

1735
01:55:54,170 --> 01:55:55,060
-They're closer than we are.

1736
01:55:55,170 --> 01:55:56,060
-I'll get the car.

1737
01:55:56,170 --> 01:55:57,360
Keys!

1738
01:56:04,040 --> 01:56:07,540
We took her to the station for safekeeping.

1739
01:56:08,380 --> 01:56:10,240
Hold her as Joan Smith.

1740
01:56:10,350 --> 01:56:12,710
And no one sees her unless I okay it.

1741
01:56:12,820 --> 01:56:14,610
Someone worked her over.

1742
01:56:14,720 --> 01:56:16,350
She wouldn't say who.

1743
01:56:21,660 --> 01:56:23,180
See you, Exley.

1744
01:56:26,430 --> 01:56:27,590
We should talk to Lynn.

1745
01:56:28,900 --> 01:56:30,560
You do it.

1746
01:56:30,670 --> 01:56:32,230
What will you do?

1747
01:56:35,070 --> 01:56:37,600
I'm going to talk to Sid Hudgens.

1748
01:56:37,710 --> 01:56:40,540
Compliment him on his performance at the Victory Motel.

1749
01:56:40,650 --> 01:56:43,880
Remember, Bud, we need evidence.

1750
01:56:43,980 --> 01:56:45,280
I'll get the evidence.

1751
01:56:58,200 --> 01:56:59,290
Are you okay?

1752
01:57:01,870 --> 01:57:03,200
You okay?

1753
01:57:13,540 --> 01:57:15,310
Bud hates himself for what he did.

1754
01:57:16,710 --> 01:57:18,510
I know how he feels.

1755
01:57:21,120 --> 01:57:23,920
I need to know what you can give me on Dudley Smith.

1756
01:57:26,060 --> 01:57:28,960
He's a police captain in business with Patchett.

1757
01:57:29,130 --> 01:57:30,490
I've never heard of him.

1758
01:57:34,800 --> 01:57:36,630
Do you have a place to stay?

1759
01:57:38,270 --> 01:57:39,500
I'll be okay.

1760
01:57:46,580 --> 01:57:48,100
Nobody goes in without official I.D.!

1761
01:57:53,480 --> 01:57:55,150
He's okay. Let him through.

1762
01:57:58,760 --> 01:58:00,450
What happened?

1763
01:58:00,560 --> 01:58:03,620
Someone beat him to death, and stole a bunch of files.

1764
01:58:03,730 --> 01:58:06,060
Must have dug up garbage on the wrong guy.

1765
01:58:06,200 --> 01:58:09,220
We got it narrowed down to 1000 suspects.

1766
01:58:09,330 --> 01:58:10,460
Sergeant White

1767
01:58:11,700 --> 01:58:13,140
dispatch got a call for you.

1768
01:58:13,240 --> 01:58:16,070
Lieutenant Exley wants you to meet him at the Victory Motel.

1769
01:58:50,680 --> 01:58:51,730
You wanted to meet here?

1770
01:58:54,250 --> 01:58:56,810
-You called it. I thought Hudgens was-- -Hudgens is dead.

1771
01:59:08,830 --> 01:59:09,880
Let's get out of here.

1772
01:59:17,800 --> 01:59:18,790
It's too late.

1773
02:00:08,650 --> 02:00:10,750
You figured it was a set-up but came anyway?

1774
02:00:10,860 --> 02:00:13,350
A lot of bad stuff happened here.

1775
02:00:13,460 --> 02:00:15,190
It's as good a place as any for it to end.

1776
02:00:25,200 --> 02:00:27,130
Clip.

1777
02:00:32,110 --> 02:00:34,540
All I ever wanted was to measure up to my father.

1778
02:00:36,010 --> 02:00:37,280
Now's your chance.

1779
02:00:39,680 --> 02:00:41,520
He died in the line of duty, didn't he?

1780
02:01:41,380 --> 02:01:42,350
Bud.

1781
02:02:41,170 --> 02:02:42,330
Goddamn it!

1782
02:03:42,600 --> 02:03:44,030
You okay?

1783
02:03:44,140 --> 02:03:45,230
Yeah.

1784
02:04:03,920 --> 02:04:05,950
Come on. Easy.

1785
02:04:12,630 --> 02:04:13,600
Move!

1786
02:04:36,190 --> 02:04:37,680
Rollo Tomasi.

1787
02:04:41,190 --> 02:04:43,130
Who is he?

1788
02:04:43,230 --> 02:04:44,460
You are.

1789
02:04:46,630 --> 02:04:48,530
You're the guy who gets away with it.

1790
02:04:52,570 --> 02:04:53,760
Jack knew it.

1791
02:04:53,870 --> 02:04:55,130
And so do l.

1792
02:05:21,070 --> 02:05:22,560
Are you going to shoot me

1793
02:05:23,970 --> 02:05:25,370
or arrest me?

1794
02:05:31,380 --> 02:05:32,360
Good lad.

1795
02:05:33,610 --> 02:05:34,980
Always the politician.

1796
02:05:36,210 --> 02:05:38,340
Let me do the talking.

1797
02:05:38,450 --> 02:05:39,680
After I'm done,

1798
02:05:39,780 --> 02:05:41,720
they'll make you Chief of Detectives.

1799
02:06:09,410 --> 02:06:11,310
Hold up your badge

1800
02:06:11,420 --> 02:06:13,110
so they'll know you're a policeman.

1801
02:07:04,170 --> 02:07:06,260
You think you can talk your way out of this, Lieutenant?

1802
02:07:09,370 --> 02:07:12,500
No but I can tell the truth.

1803
02:07:13,340 --> 02:07:19,570
During our investigation of events surrounding the Nite Owl case

1804
02:07:20,520 --> 02:07:24,720
Jack Vincennes, Bud White and I learned the following:

1805
02:07:24,820 --> 02:07:27,310
Your golden boy's throwing his whole life away.

1806
02:07:27,420 --> 02:07:29,790
The 3 Nite Owl suspects

1807
02:07:29,890 --> 02:07:33,020
while guilty of kidnapping and rape

1808
02:07:33,130 --> 02:07:35,790
were innocent of the multiple homicides at the Nite Owl.

1809
02:07:37,470 --> 02:07:39,490
The gunmen were most likely

1810
02:07:39,600 --> 02:07:44,510
Los Angeles police officers Michael Breuning and William Carlisle

1811
02:07:44,610 --> 02:07:46,770
and a third man

1812
02:07:46,880 --> 02:07:50,240
who may or may not have been Captain Dudley Smith.

1813
02:07:51,620 --> 02:07:52,880
The objective:

1814
02:07:54,020 --> 02:07:56,610
The elimination of another police officer

1815
02:07:56,750 --> 02:07:58,310
Richard Stensland

1816
02:07:59,560 --> 02:08:04,820
who, along with former LAPD officer Leland "Buzz" Meeks

1817
02:08:05,630 --> 02:08:08,890
also committed multiple homicides on behalf of Captain Smith

1818
02:08:09,970 --> 02:08:15,060
and then betrayed him over 25 pounds of heroin

1819
02:08:15,170 --> 02:08:17,270
the retrieval of which

1820
02:08:17,370 --> 02:08:19,870
was the ultimate motivation behind the Nite Owl killings.

1821
02:08:23,580 --> 02:08:27,140
Beginning with the incarceration of Mickey Cohen

1822
02:08:27,250 --> 02:08:32,850
Capt. Smith has been assuming control of organized crime in Los Angeles.

1823
02:08:32,960 --> 02:08:38,360
This includes the assassinations of Mickey Cohen lieutenants

1824
02:08:38,460 --> 02:08:43,130
the systematic blackmail of city officials

1825
02:08:43,230 --> 02:08:45,220
and the murders of Susan Lefferts,

1826
02:08:45,340 --> 02:08:47,300
Pierce Patchett, Sid Hudgens

1827
02:08:49,110 --> 02:08:50,940
and Sergeant Jack Vincennes.

1828
02:08:54,480 --> 02:08:57,780
Captain Smith admitted as much to me

1829
02:08:57,880 --> 02:09:02,080
before I shot him at the Victory Motel.

1830
02:09:04,320 --> 02:09:05,410
That's it.

1831
02:09:07,730 --> 02:09:12,420
Well the press will have a field day.

1832
02:09:13,960 --> 02:09:18,000
Christ! It'll stain the Department for years.

1833
02:09:18,040 --> 02:09:19,260
Decades.

1834
02:09:20,340 --> 02:09:22,830
If we can get the kid to play ball

1835
02:09:23,940 --> 02:09:25,430
who's to say what happened?

1836
02:09:26,840 --> 02:09:29,540
Maybe Dudley Smith died a hero.

1837
02:09:29,650 --> 02:09:32,440
-Good idea. -lf we get the press to play.

1838
02:09:40,060 --> 02:09:42,460
Want to tell me what you're smiling about?

1839
02:09:48,200 --> 02:09:49,260
A hero.

1840
02:09:50,130 --> 02:09:51,860
How'd he know what we said?

1841
02:09:52,140 --> 02:09:53,400
He couldn't have heard us.

1842
02:09:57,370 --> 02:09:59,670
In this situation

1843
02:09:59,780 --> 02:10:01,270
you'll need more than one.

1844
02:10:08,420 --> 02:10:11,510
It is my pleasure to present this award to

1845
02:10:11,620 --> 02:10:16,290
Detective Lieutenant Edmund Exley two-time Medal of Valor recipient.

1846
02:10:26,340 --> 02:10:29,790
Next year the LAPD will move into its new facility.

1847
02:10:30,840 --> 02:10:32,540
With leaders like Edmund Exley

1848
02:10:32,640 --> 02:10:35,980
the image of fat cops stealing apples will be left behind

1849
02:10:36,080 --> 02:10:39,540
and Los Angeles will finally have the police force it deserves.

1850
02:10:53,830 --> 02:10:55,990
You just couldn't resist.

1851
02:10:56,100 --> 02:10:58,470
They're using me. So for a while, I'm using them.

1852
02:11:00,800 --> 02:11:01,830
Come on.

1853
02:11:36,840 --> 02:11:38,000
Thanks for the push.

1854
02:11:59,660 --> 02:12:01,320
Congratulations, Lieutenant Exley.

1855
02:12:05,170 --> 02:12:07,690
Some men get the world

1856
02:12:07,800 --> 02:12:11,040
others get ex-hookers and a trip to Arizona.

